  "history": null,
  "answer": "Under KCERA’s **minimum qualifications** for audit services, the firm must:\n\n- Be a professional public accounting firm organized at least regionally and providing audit and other attest services.\n- Have completed **at least five audits in the past five years** of defined-benefit pension plans with assets exceeding **$2 billion**.\n- Have experience auditing domestic and foreign equities, fixed income, real estate, alternative investments, commodities, and securities lending.\n- Have an established U.S. office and be independent, licensed, and in good standing in California.\n- Assign a U.S.-based engagement partner—and, if different, opinion-signing partner—with at least **10 years** of public-accounting experience including defined-benefit pension audits, and a California CPA license in good standing.\n- Assign a U.S.-based engagement manager with at least **five years** of public-accounting experience including such audits, and a CPA license in good standing in a U.S. state.\n- Assign a U.S.-based on-site supervisor with at least **three years** of professional auditing experience including such audits, and a CPA license in good standing in a U.S. state. The manager and supervisor must be available for consultations and in-person meetings throughout the year.\n\nSource: KCERA *RFP for Audit Services*, Attachment 2, “Minimum and Desirable Qualifications Certification,” pp. 29–30.",
